While she (or he) can look at your .newsrc file, she shouldn't look at
it without giving you notice. The .newsrc file is a file in your home
directory. I can think of no legitimate reason for a system admin to
*secretly* look at this file.

Such a suspensionless search might be unconsitutional at a state
university. Even at most all private U.S. universities, if she looks
at what you read than then blabs it to those with no need to know, she
may be violating the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act.

- Carl

